{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2215","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. RReeppeettiittiioonn"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2.5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As a girl born on November 11th (or 11/11), SS loves repetition. For example, her favorite English word is b"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ookkee"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"per, her favorite letter is W (double-u, double vé, or whatever you call it), her favorite animals are the cat (ki"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tt"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"en!) and the ra"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"it (bu"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nn"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"y!), her favorite programming language is C"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"++"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", her favorite parser is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LL"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1), her favorite optimization algorithm is branch and bound ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"BB"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"), her favorite unit is millimeter ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mm"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"), her favorite game is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LLLL"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and her favorite winning hand in Mahjong is Seven Pairs. She plans to release her new songs \"Silent-night Satellite\" and \"Siesta Stella\" soon, so she wants to select a \"pre"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tt"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"y\" number to decorate the cover of her new songs."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"SS observes this world from a higher perspective, which means she considers an integer concurrently in all standard positional numeral systems, starting from the binary numeral system. SS then calls a positive integer $$$n$$$ $$$(b, p)$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-tidy"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (with $$$b,p\\ge 2$$$) if and only if:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" In base-$$$b$$$ representation, $$$n$$$ is represented as $$$\\overline{d_{k\\cdot p-1} d_{k\\cdot p-2}\\ldots d_1 d_0}$$$ for some positive integer $$$k$$$ and integers $$$0\\le d_i \\lt b$$$, such that for each $$$0\\le i \\lt k$$$, $$$d_{i\\cdot p}=d_{i\\cdot p+1}=\\cdots=d_{(i+1)\\cdot p-1}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, $$$2233$$$ and $$$3355$$$ are $$$(10,2)$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-tidy"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", $$$1111$$$ is both $$$(10,2)$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-tidy"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and $$$(10,4)$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-tidy"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and $$$6\\,737\\,151=(66\\textrm{CCFF})_{16}$$$ is $$$(16,2)$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-tidy"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Furthermore, SS defines the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tidiness"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of a positive integer $$$n$$$ as the number of ordered pairs $$$(b, p)$$$ such that $$$n$$$ is $$$(b, p)$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-tidy"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"SS has given you an integer $$$n$$$. Your task is to determine the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tidiness"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 1000$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1\\le n\\le 10^{12}$$$) — the integer SS has given you."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$10^{12}$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tidiness"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n10\n1\n2\n115\n1111\n2233\n3355\n191970\n6737151\n102934760424\n618111100000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n0\n2\n4\n5\n5\n24\n9\n17\n144\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, $$$115={(55)}_{22}={(11)}_{114}$$$. Therefore, the tidiness of $$$115$$$ is $$$2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth test case, $$$1111$$$ is $$$(10, 2)$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-tidy"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", $$$(10, 4)$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-tidy"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", $$$(100, 2)$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-tidy"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and $$$(1110, 2)$$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-tidy"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"2215B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2215/problem/B"}